## Summary

`BlobSource::load_blobs` in kona's derivation pipeline is missing a post-loop over-fill check. After the fill loop completes, if the blob provider returned more blobs than were requested (i.e. `blob_index < blobs.len()`), kona silently discards the extra blobs with no error. The Go op-node reference implementation treats this condition as a Reset-level error.

## Go Reference Behaviour

In `op-node`, `fillBlobPointers` at [`blob_data_source.go:162-164`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/9eaad92f7f2f8a5f9687b6a703d4afc3dad1d347/op-node/rollup/derive/blob_data_source.go#L162) performs this check after the fill loop:

```go
if blobIndex != len(blobs) {
    return fmt.Errorf("got too many blobs")
}
```

This error is then wrapped as `NewResetError` at the call site (`blob_data_source.go:110`), causing the pipeline to reset and retry rather than silently accepting a malformed provider response.

## Kona Subject Location

[`blobs.rs:164-173`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/9eaad92f7f2f8a5f9687b6a703d4afc3dad1d347/rust/kona/crates/protocol/derive/src/sources/blobs.rs#L164) — the fill loop ends at line 173 with no subsequent check:

```rust
// Fill the blob pointers.
let mut blob_index = 0;
for blob in &mut data {
    let should_increment = blob
        .fill(&blobs, blob_index)
        .map_err(|e| -> PipelineErrorKind { e.into() })?;
    if should_increment {
        blob_index += 1;
    }
}
// ← no check that blob_index == blobs.len() here
```

## When This Can Occur

While uncommon, this situation can arise in practice:

- **Buggy L1 providers**: A beacon/blob provider that returns more blobs than requested (not spec-compliant but not unheard-of with third-party providers).
- **L1 reorgs**: In rare reorg scenarios the set of blob transactions referenced by an L1 block can shift between the time the hashes are collected and the time the blobs are fetched, resulting in a count mismatch.

## Proposed Fix

After the fill loop in `load_blobs`, add a post-loop check:

```rust
if blob_index < blobs.len() {
    return Err(ResetError::BlobsOverFill(blob_index, blobs.len()).reset());
}
```

A new `ResetError::BlobsOverFill(usize, usize)` variant should be added (symmetric to the existing `BlobsUnderFill` variant), mapping to `PipelineErrorKind::Reset`. This mirrors `op-node`'s `NewResetError` wrapping and ensures the pipeline resets and retries rather than silently accepting an inconsistent provider response.

## References

- Subject: https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/9eaad92f7f2f8a5f9687b6a703d4afc3dad1d347/rust/kona/crates/protocol/derive/src/sources/blobs.rs#L164
- Reference: https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/9eaad92f7f2f8a5f9687b6a703d4afc3dad1d347/op-node/rollup/derive/blob_data_source.go#L162

