## Summary

- Adds high-level DSL methods to `DerivationTest` (`advance_l1`, `derive_empty_block`, `submit_batch`, `finalize`) that describe test scenarios rather than implementation details
- Adds `BatchConfig` with sensible defaults and `BlockBuilder` with `with_funded_transfer()` for simple ETH transfers
- Rewrites all happy-path tests to 3-5 lines; adversarial tests use DSL for setup, drop to low-level only for the adversarial part
- Deletes `tests/helpers/` — both `default_test()` and `funded_signer()` are replaced by DSL methods

Before:
```rust
test.l1.emit_empty_block();
test.l1.emit_empty_block();
let l1_block = test.l1.block_at(1).unwrap().clone();
test.l2.set_epoch(&l1_block);
let block_ref = test.l2.build_empty_block().unwrap();
let batch = test.singular_batch_calldata(&[block_ref], &l1_block);
test.l1.emit_block_with_batches(vec![batch]);
```

After:
```rust
test.advance_l1(2);
test.derive_empty_block();
test.submit_batch_with(BatchConfig::singular_calldata());
```

## Test plan

- [x] All 41 non-integration tests pass (`cargo test -p derivation-tests --test simple --test invalid --test server --lib`)
- [x] `cargo clippy -p derivation-tests --tests -- -D warnings` passes clean
- [x] `cargo fmt -p derivation-tests -- --check` passes clean
- [x] Golden super root values updated (auto-epoch to genesis changes roots)
- [ ] Integration tests with op-program and kona-host (requires binary builds)

